From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:48:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 322/488] CED requests: switch to the TileLang kernel with
 per-request row limits and remove the old one

CEDState stages each request's kept-row limit, 2^31-1 for a request that keeps
every row and the 128-row window otherwise, in place of the bool keep_full, and
stages its metadata with the TileLang requests kernel. Its three
specializations (unchanged rows, one request compacted, several) are declared
with the row map, so they compile before the cache freezes. With those two
limit values the outputs are identical to the Triton kernel's; per-request
limits are the interface the CED skip needs. The Triton kernel is removed; the
benchmark and the kernel tests keep their copy as the reference.
